1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Welcome to Resume Customizer AI — an intelligent, full-stack application

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
that tailors candidate resumes to target job descriptions while enforcing strict anti-fabrication standards.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Most generative tools hallucinate unearned credentials or metrics to beat Applicant Tracking Systems.

4
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:32,300
Resume Customizer AI strategically aligns genuine candidate accomplishments without ever inventing false experience.

5
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:38,500
The application architecture is modern, resilient, and production-tested.

6
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:47,000
The frontend is built on Next.js 16 with the React 19 App Router, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS version 4,

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,500
styled in an editorial Aubergine and Copper theme.

8
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:01,500
The backend is a high-performance Python 3.11 asynchronous microservice powered by FastAPI and Uvicorn.

9
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:09,500
Document processing is executed server-side via PyPDF, python-docx, and ReportLab Platypus.

10
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:16,500
Database persistence and authentication run on managed Supabase PostgreSQL with Row Level Security,

11
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,990
while the intelligence layer integrates Google Gemini with deterministic heuristic fallbacks.

12
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:27,500
Starting on our live production application deployed on Vercel, we upload a resume document.

13
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:34,000
Our ingestion pipeline supports both Adobe PDF and Microsoft Word DOCX files.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,000
For this walkthrough, we are using a synthetic candidate profile: Alex Morgan, a Staff Full Stack Engineer.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:49,500
The backend parser enforces a five-megabyte size ceiling, validates document streams,

16
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:58,880
strips dangerous control characters, and extracts both paragraphs and tables into normalized Unicode text.

17
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:06,500
Next, we enter a target Job Description for a Senior Backend and Cloud Infrastructure Engineer position.

18
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:14,500
The application validates the job description in real time, requiring at least fifty characters for keyword extraction.

19
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:22,500
Notice the granular section controls beneath the input. Candidates can independently toggle whether

20
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:31,040
the AI customizes the Professional Summary, aligns the Skills taxonomy, or rephrases Experience bullets.

21
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:38,000
Clicking Tailor Resume initiates an asynchronous workflow to our FastAPI backend on Render.

22
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:46,000
A live six-stage progress tracker visualizes the analysis: reading document structure, parsing target competencies,

23
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:54,500
evaluating multi-factor ATS alignment, generating evidence-grounded optimizations, verifying factual integrity,

24
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:03,050
and assembling the studio workspace. In production, this completes in under nine seconds.

25
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:09,500
Once processed, we enter the Interactive Resume Studio.

26
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:17,500
The resume is presented in an executive typography layout with clear section badges and bullet formatting.

27
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:24,000
Every field is fully editable inline. Candidates can refine their summary, adjust bullets, or add verified skills.

28
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Clicking the Re-check Score button instantly recalculates ATS compatibility and match breakdown,

29
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:36,600
providing real-time feedback on how manual edits affect recruiter screening.

30
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:43,500
Switching to the ATS and Alignment Audit tab reveals our transparent evaluation dashboard.

31
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:52,000
Unlike black-box algorithms, Resume Customizer AI displays an objective weighted score: thirty-five percent for required skills,

32
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:00,500
fifteen percent for preferred skills, fifteen percent for experience, fifteen percent for responsibilities,

33
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:08,000
and ten percent each for domain keywords and formatting structure.

34
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:15,380
The heuristic audit grades technical parseability, readability, and reverse-chronological layout.

35
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:23,000
Here we see the core differentiator of our application: the isolated Skill-Gap Analysis panel.

36
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Rather than hallucinating missing requirements into the resume, absent skills such as Kafka or Prometheus

37
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:38,500
are quarantined into this dedicated advisory section.

38
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:46,140
Candidates receive actionable recommendations on how to legitimately acquire or demonstrate these skills.

39
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:54,000
In the Change Diff Analysis tab, candidates can review a side-by-side comparison between original and tailored drafts.

40
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:01,500
This highlights how bullet points were rephrased with strong action verbs while preserving factual claims.

41
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:08,500
The application also generates an executive cover letter aligned with genuine qualifications,

42
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:15,460
complete with one-click clipboard copying and letterhead PDF download.

43
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:23,000
When ready, candidates can export their tailored resume in three production-ready formats:

44
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:31,000
an ATS-standard PDF generated with ReportLab, an editable Word DOCX file, or clean plain text.

45
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:39,500
Resume Customizer AI demonstrates full-stack software craftsmanship, combining Next.js, FastAPI, Supabase, and Gemini.

46
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:47,000
The code and test suites are open source on GitHub, and the live application is deployed on Vercel and Render.

47
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:52,970
Thank you for watching!

